.TH TENSOR-GPU-WALLPAPER-ARBITER 1 "2026-11-24" "Tensor GPU lifecycle" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tensor-gpu-wallpaper-arbiter \- source-only atomic wallpaper startup contract
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tensor-gpu-wallpaper-arbiter.py
.RI [ --help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Provides a Python callback API for a future guarded wallpaper unit. It uses the
same private gpu-lease.lock flock as the Tensor GPU lease manager and verifies
the SQLite lease state while holding that lock, then calls the injected launch
and readiness callbacks before releasing it. Non-normal, unverified and busy
state refuses startup. It cannot start a service via its command-line interface.
.SH SAFETY
Do not install as a live Wallpaper Engine systemd ExecStart until a Type=notify
supervisor wrapper and two-phase restore protocol are implemented and tested.
The current LeaseManager restoration holds the lease lock during systemctl start;
a naive unit wrapper waiting for that lock could otherwise deadlock. This library
uses a nonblocking lock to refuse rather than hang, but restoration would remain
pending without a proper handoff. This is not production admission authorization.
.SH SOURCE
shared/scripts/tensor-gpu-wallpaper-arbiter.py in iragonforce/ops.
